WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.292
TIMESTAMPTZ is PostgreSQL's timestamp with time zone
type Conceptually

00:00:06.516 --> 00:00:12.103
it represents an instant PostgreSQL can display that
instant in

00:00:12.129 --> 00:00:18.128
different time zones This is useful for events
collected across locations

00:00:19.871 --> 00:00:24.200
The key distinction is between the stored instant
and the clock representation shown to a

00:00:24.226 --> 00:00:24.726
user
